civetweb 1.16, vendored for bepsi-httpd.

Source:   https://github.com/civetweb/civetweb  tag v1.16
Tarball:  civetweb-1.16.tar.gz
SHA-256:  f0e471c1bf4e7804a6cfb41ea9d13e7d623b2bcc7bc1e2a4dd54951a24d60285
License:  MIT; see LICENSE.md (CREDITS.md lists the authors).

Why vendored: bepsi wants a single-binary HTTPS server with CGI, built against
the machine's OpenSSL 3.  Debian's civetweb 1.16 package segfaults on the first
TLS request (checked on Debian 13 with OpenSSL 3.5), and it forwards CGI output
only when the script exits, so it cannot stream.  Building this source with
-DOPENSSL_API_3_0 -DNO_SSL_DL gives a ~200 KB binary that serves TLS 1.2/1.3.

Files kept: civetweb.c, civetweb.h, main.c (the stand-alone server) and the
.inl files they include for this build (sort, match, response, timer,
handle_form, openssl_dl, md5, sha1).  Lua, Duktape, mbedTLS, wolfSSL, zlib and
HTTP/2 sources are left out.

Local modifications: none.  List any here, with the reason, as they are made.
